From bb26e50cfeb8d50d282036736958159e784799f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:48:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] [dxgi] Bind composition swap chains to DComp windows

Swap chains created through CreateSwapChainForComposition present to a
hidden dummy window, and the option that enables them defaults to off
because nothing ever showed up on screen. The only reason to enable it
so far has been games that probe the API, which ship per-game profiles
for that purpose.

Wine's dcomp implementation needs the opposite. It creates a host
window for each visual that carries a swap chain and has to tell DXVK
to present there. Add a private IDXGIVkCompositionSwapChain interface
with a single SetCompositionTarget(HWND target, HWND dispatch) method,
exposed by composition swap chains only. The target is the window to
present to and the dispatch window is the top-level window that owns
the visual tree; both are equal when the swap chain covers that window
itself. A null target returns the swap chain to its dummy window. Wine
consumes the interface through its IID and vtable layout, so both are
part of the ABI.

Binding retargets the surface factory before destroying the presenter's
resources, so that a concurrent acquire cannot recreate the surface on
the old window before the presenter picks up the new one. The factory
keeps its dummy window alive for the lifetime of the swap chain rather
than destroying and recreating it around every bind: DestroyWindow only
works from the creating thread, and binds arrive on Wine's dcomp commit
thread rather than the thread that created the swap chain.

The WSI surface stays opaque regardless of the DXGI alpha mode. The
alpha mode remains in the swap chain description for the compositor's
placement logic, but the host window is blended against its parent by
the desktop compositor, and honouring premultiplied alpha there erases
otherwise correct frames against a dark parent window.

Enable the option by default, which subsumes the existing per-game
profiles that only turned it on, and downgrade the message for the
disabled case to a warning since that is now a configuration choice.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
